  "transcriptText": "Welcome to the Rules. This is how a hand plays... and it all starts with the deck. So, a question. Your ace of spades, against their ace of hearts. Whose is better? Spades, hearts... or neither?\n\nLet's sort the deck. Four suits. Spades, hearts, diamonds and clubs. Each suit has thirteen ranks, from two all the way up to ace. Four times thirteen... fifty-two cards. And no jokers. Not in this game.\n\nRanks are what count. The ace is the highest card... but it has one trick. It can also play low, in one straight. Ace, two, three, four, five. The lowest straight there is.\n\nNow, back to your aces. Here's a showdown. The board runs queen, jack, ten, four, three. You hold ace-king. So do they. You both make the same straight, ace down to ten. Your spade doesn't beat their heart... so the pot splits. A hundred each.\n\nSo the answer is neither. No suit beats another. Suits only matter for one thing... a flush. Five cards of the same suit. Thirteen ranks, four suits. Ranks decide. Up next: the hand rankings."
